{"notes":"## Full Implementation Plan (with code)

### Step 1: Source package struct rename + add Depositor
```go
type GoldenBraidContext struct {
    Name         string
    Summary      string
    Genes        O.Option[[]string]
    Publications O.Option[[]string]
    User         string        // was UserEmail in old GoldenBraidContext
    PlasmidType  string        // was PlasmidCV in old GoldenBraidContext
    Depositor    string        // NEW — from CLI --depositor flag
    CreatedOn    time.Time
    UpdatedOn    time.Time
}
```

### Step 1: BuildGoldenBraidContext (replaces BuildPlasmid)
```go
func BuildGoldenBraidContext(
    userEmail, plasmidCVTerm, depositor string,
) func([]string) *GoldenBraidContext {
    return func(r []string) *GoldenBraidContext {
        now := time.Now()
        return &GoldenBraidContext{
            Name:         strings.TrimSpace(r[0]),
            Summary:      strings.TrimSpace(r[5]),
            Genes:        parseCommaSeparatedField(r[3]),
            Publications: parsePublicationField(r[6]),
            User:         userEmail,
            PlasmidType:  plasmidCVTerm,
            Depositor:    depositor,
            CreatedOn:    now,
            UpdatedOn:    now,
        }
    }
}
```

### Step 3b: buildNewPlasmidRequest (flattened field access)
```go
func buildNewPlasmidRequest(ctx *source.GoldenBraidContext) *stock.NewPlasmid {
    return &stock.NewPlasmid{
        Data: &stock.NewPlasmid_Data{
            Type: "plasmid",
            Attributes: &stock.NewPlasmidAttributes{
                Name:                 ctx.Name,
                CreatedBy:            ctx.User,
                UpdatedBy:            ctx.User,
                Depositor:            ctx.Depositor,
                Summary:              ctx.Summary,
                Genes:                O.GetOrElse(F.Constant([]string{}))(ctx.Genes),
                Publications:         O.GetOrElse(F.Constant([]string{}))(ctx.Publications),
                DictyPlasmidProperty: ctx.PlasmidType,
            },
        },
    }
}
```

### Step 3c: fetchPlasmidByName (simple string-based)
```go
func fetchPlasmidByName(name string) IOE.IOEither[error, O.Option[*stock.Plasmid]] {
    return F.Pipe2(
        IOE.TryCatchError(func() (*stock.PlasmidCollection, error) {
            return regsc.GetStockAPIClient().ListPlasmids(
                context.Background(),
                &stock.StockParameters{
                    Filter: fmt.Sprintf("plasmid_name===%s", name),
                    Limit:  1,
                },
            )
        }),
        IOE.MapLeft[*stock.PlasmidCollection](func(err error) error {
            return fmt.Errorf("failed to fetch plasmid %s: %w", name, err)
        }),
        IOE.Map[error](collectionToOption),
    )
}
```

### Step 3d: fetchAndResolve (merges fetch + O.Fold)
```go
func fetchAndResolve(ctx *source.GoldenBraidContext) IOE.IOEither[error, GoldenBraidUpsertResult] {
    return F.Pipe1(
        fetchPlasmidByName(ctx.Name),
        IOE.Chain(O.Fold(createNewPlasmid(ctx), skipExistingPlasmid)),
    )
}
```

### Step 3g: processPlasmidWithUpsert (flat, point-free)
```go
